; E2E audit profile (P1-T05), copied from the S10 profile (P0-S10-T1): everything allowed except non-loopback network and DNS. A process that attempts either is
; killed (SIGKILL), so one attempt cannot go unnoticed; the kernel's denial log is kept only as a hint, because it
; drops reports (8 of 12 identical attempts were logged on macOS 27.2). fixtures.ts strips the modifier for the one
; NetLog control, which needs the process to survive its denied attempt.
; Order matters (verified on macOS 27.2): the loopback allow must come last, or loopback is denied too.
(version 1)
(allow default)
; DNS goes through this socket: denied, so a lookup counts as an attempt.
(deny network-outbound (remote unix-socket (path-literal "/private/var/run/mDNSResponder")) (with send-signal SIGKILL)) ; privacy-scan:allow system socket, not a home path
(deny network-outbound (remote ip "*:*") (with send-signal SIGKILL))
(allow network-outbound (remote ip "localhost:*"))
